{0 UTF-8 parsing}

{!module:Parseff.Utf8} provides primitives operating on Unicode code points
([Uchar.t]) decoded from UTF-8 [string] input, backed by
{{:https://erratique.ch/software/uucp}uucp} for Unicode character properties.

Primitives operate at the code-point level (a base character plus combining
mark is two code points). For grapheme clusters, compose them with a library
such as {{:https://erratique.ch/software/uuseg}uuseg}.

{1 Primitives}

{@ocaml skip[
val satisfy : ?label:string -> (Uchar.t -> bool) -> Uchar.t
val char : Uchar.t -> Uchar.t
val any_char : unit -> Uchar.t
val take_while : ?at_least:int -> ?label:string -> (Uchar.t -> bool) -> string
val skip_while : ?at_least:int -> ?label:string -> (Uchar.t -> bool) -> unit

module Slice : sig
  val take_while : ?at_least:int -> ?label:string -> (Uchar.t -> bool) -> Slice.t
end
]}

- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.satisfy} decodes the next code point (1–4 bytes) and tests
  the predicate, failing with [expected <label>] (default
  ["matching character"]).
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.char} matches an exact [Uchar.t].
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.any_char} decodes and returns the next code point, failing
  at EOF or on invalid UTF-8.
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.take_while} consumes code points while the predicate holds
  and returns the matched UTF-8 string. [~at_least] counts {e code points}, not
  bytes.
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.skip_while} skips matching code points without allocating.
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.Slice.take_while} returns a zero-copy
  {!type:Parseff.Slice.t}.
- All three take [~at_least] and [~label], with the same failure.

{1 Mixing with byte-level primitives}

UTF-8 and byte-level primitives mix freely in the same parser: use byte-level
primitives for ASCII syntax and {!module:Parseff.Utf8} for text content.

{@ocaml[
let field () =
  let key =
    Parseff.take_while ~at_least:1 ~label:"key" (fun c -> c >= 'a' && c <= 'z')
  in
  Parseff.literal ":";
  Parseff.Utf8.skip_whitespace ();
  let value =
    Parseff.Utf8.take_while ~at_least:1 ~label:"value" (fun u ->
        Uchar.to_int u <> 0x0A)
  in
  (key, value)

let lambda () = Parseff.Utf8.char (Uchar.of_int 0x03BB)
]}

{1 Convenience combinators}

{@ocaml skip[
val letter : unit -> Uchar.t
val alphanum : unit -> Uchar.t
val is_whitespace : Uchar.t -> bool
val whitespace : ?at_least:int -> unit -> string
val skip_whitespace : unit -> unit
]}

- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.letter}: matches Unicode alphabetic code points
  ([Uucp.Alpha.is_alphabetic] across Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, CJK, Arabic,
  Devanagari, etc.).
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.alphanum}: matches a Unicode alphabetic code point or
  ASCII digit.
- {!val:Parseff.Utf8.is_whitespace}, {!val:Parseff.Utf8.whitespace}, and
  {!val:Parseff.Utf8.skip_whitespace}: match the Unicode [White_Space] property
  ([Uucp.White.is_white_space], including [U+00A0], [U+2002], [U+2003],
  [U+3000]). [~at_least] on [whitespace] counts code points.

{1 Invalid UTF-8}

All [Utf8] primitives fail with [expected valid UTF-8] on bare continuation
bytes ([0x80]–[0xBF]), invalid lead bytes ([0xFE], [0xFF]), overlong encodings,
and truncated sequences, pointing at the first invalid byte
([expected valid UTF-8, found '\xFF']). Invalid UTF-8 always reports
[valid UTF-8] regardless of [~label].

{1 Positions, columns, and streaming}

- {b Positions}: {!val:Parseff.position} and [location.byte_col] always count
  bytes (a single [Utf8.satisfy] advances by 1–4 bytes).
- {b Error columns and carets}: {!val:Parseff.render_error} header columns
  count code points, while carets count terminal cells (wide characters like
  [名] take two, combining marks take zero). See {!page:errors} for streaming
  dropped-prefix behavior.

{v
input.json:1:6: [error] expected ',' or ']', found '"'
1 | ["é" "b"]
  |      ^
v}

- {b Streaming}: all [Utf8] primitives work across chunk boundaries in
  {!val:Parseff.Source.parse} and {!module:Parseff.Push}.
